From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rust-mos-sync <rust-mos-sync@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:51:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [MOS] Adapt to the LLVM API of the rustc/23.1 branch

- TargetMachine::resetTargetOptions was removed upstream; per-function code
  generation flags no longer live in TargetOptions, so there is nothing to
  reset before creating a subtarget.
- MCTargetAsmParser and the MCAsmParser constructor registered by
  RegisterMCAsmParser no longer take MCTargetOptions.
- GlobalISel: G_CTLZ/CTTZ_ZERO_UNDEF became _ZERO_POISON, the legacy legalizer
  tables are gone (no computeTables), and LegalizerHelper::lowerMemcpyInline
  is folded into lowerMemCpyFamily (which handles G_MEMCPY_INLINE).
- The legacy tables also made opcodes without type operands legal by default:
  G_BR now needs an explicit alwaysLegal().
- TargetMachine::getMCAsmInfo returns a reference, and
  MCStreamer::emitCodeAlignment takes the subtarget by reference.
- MCAsmInfoELF has no default constructor: it takes the MCTargetOptions.
- -gen-callingconv output is guarded by GET_CALLING_CONV_IMPL now.
- The prologepilog pass is called prolog-epilog (two MIR tests' RUN lines).
- all_combines gained select_zero_false (select c, x, 0 -> and c, freeze x),
  whose generated apply code builds an s1 G_AND without checking legality;
  MOS has no such instruction, so the rule is disabled in MOSCombiner.
